# User Profile — AI Context
#
# Copy to docs/USER_PROFILE.md (gitignored) and fill in your own details.
# Loaded by AI at session start to calibrate communication and behavior.

## Who I am
# 2-4 sentences. Role, domain knowledge, relationship to this codebase.
# AI uses this to understand how much context to give and what to assume.
[Your role and company]. [Years of experience and career path].
[Your relationship to this project — owner, contractor, contributor].
[What you know from the inside — so AI doesn't need to explain it back to you].
[Optional: career goal or direction].

## Projects
# List all active projects with priority order.
# AI uses this to understand context when scope is ambiguous.
# Mark which project this profile belongs to with "Ten projekt".
1. **[Project name]** — [one sentence description]. [Stack if relevant]. [Priority note if needed].
2. **[Project name]** — [one sentence description].
3. **[This project]** — [one sentence description].
   **Ten projekt** — AI czyta ten profil w kontekście [this project name].

## Experience level
# Per area. AI uses this to decide how much to explain.
# Levels: beginner | intermediate | senior | expert
Backend ([languages/frameworks]):  [level]
Frontend ([languages/frameworks]): [level]
Mobile ([frameworks]):             [level]
Bazy danych ([databases]):         [level]
DevOps / Docker:                   [level]
Architektura systemów:             [level]

## Communication
# Hard rules for every response. AI treats these as non-negotiable.
Language:      [polski / English / ...]
Tone:          [direct / formal / casual]
Explanations:  [senior-level / explain basics / somewhere in between]
Openers:       [none / ok to use]
Summaries:     [none at end of response / ok to use]
Emojis:        [never / ok]
Role AI:       [sparring partner / assistant / rubber duck / ...]

## Decisions
# How AI should present options and recommendations.
Default:   [one recommendation with reason / list of options / ...]
Pushback:  [yes, say clearly when something is wrong / no, just do what I ask]
"Zależy":  [only when a specific fact is missing / ...]

## Never do this
# Patterns that cause friction. AI treats these as blockers.
- [e.g. Native alert()/confirm()/prompt()]
- [e.g. Inline date formatting — use the project's central format lib]
- [e.g. Guessing business logic — ask when unsure]
- [e.g. Implementing "for the future" without a current use case]

## Always do this
# Patterns you've validated and want applied consistently.
- [e.g. Result<T> for business errors, exceptions for infrastructure errors]
- [e.g. Tests written alongside code, not after]
- [e.g. One commit = one closed step (code + docs together)]
- [e.g. No hardcoded values — env vars or config from day 1]
